---
// Ill08ThreeIdentities.astro
// Visual brief: Three Identities — Economic Owner vs Legal Holder vs Tax Interface
---

<div class="my-10 bg-slate-50 dark:bg-navy-900/90 border border-slate-200 dark:border-navy-800 rounded-xl overflow-hidden shadow-sm not-prose font-sans w-full max-w-2xl mx-auto">
  <div class="px-6 py-4 border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-navy-800 bg-slate-100/60 dark:bg-navy-950/60 flex items-center justify-between">
    <div>
      <div class="text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-indigo-600 dark:text-indigo-400 font-semibold">Editorial Visual 08</div>
      <h3 class="text-base text-slate-900 dark:text-white font-semibold m-0">The Three Identities of ₹100 Income</h3>
    </div>
    <span class="text-xs font-mono px-2.5 py-1 bg-indigo-500/10 text-indigo-600 dark:text-indigo-400 rounded border border-indigo-500/20 font-medium">CBDT 13/2014</span>
  </div>

  <div class="p-6">
    <div class="space-y-4">
      <!-- Identity 1 -->
      <div class="p-4 rounded-lg bg-white dark:bg-navy-800/60 border border-blue-200 dark:border-blue-800/50 flex items-center gap-4">
        <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-full bg-blue-100 dark:bg-blue-900/40 text-blue-700 dark:text-blue-300 flex items-center justify-center font-mono font-bold text-sm shrink-0">
          01
        </div>
        <div class="flex-1">
          <div class="text-xs font-semibold text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400 uppercase tracking-wider">Economic Owner</div>
          <div class="text-sm font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">The Beneficiary (Unit Holder)</div>
          <div class="text-xs text-slate-500 mt-0.5">Entitled to economic upside, absorbs market drawdown, funds capital.</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Identity 2 -->
      <div class="p-4 rounded-lg bg-white dark:bg-navy-800/60 border border-amber-200 dark:border-amber-800/50 flex items-center gap-4">
        <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-full bg-amber-100 dark:bg-amber-900/40 text-amber-700 dark:text-amber-300 flex items-center justify-center font-mono font-bold text-sm shrink-0">
          02
        </div>
        <div class="flex-1">
          <div class="text-xs font-semibold text-amber-600 dark:text-amber-400 uppercase tracking-wider">Legal Holder</div>
          <div class="text-sm font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">The Trustee</div>
          <div class="text-xs text-slate-500 mt-0.5">Holds the property in trust, executes agreements, regulatory counterparty.</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Identity 3 -->
      <div class="p-4 rounded-lg bg-white dark:bg-navy-800/60 border border-indigo-200 dark:border-indigo-800/50 flex items-center gap-4">
        <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-full bg-indigo-100 dark:bg-indigo-900/40 text-indigo-700 dark:text-indigo-300 flex items-center justify-center font-mono font-bold text-sm shrink-0">
          03
        </div>
        <div class="flex-1">
          <div class="text-xs font-semibold text-indigo-600 dark:text-indigo-400 uppercase tracking-wider">Tax Interface</div>
          <div class="text-sm font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Representative Assessee (Trustee on behalf of Beneficiary)</div>
          <div class="text-xs text-slate-500 mt-0.5">Assessed under Sections 160–164 (or MMR if indeterminate) to prevent dual taxation.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="px-6 py-3 bg-slate-100/50 dark:bg-navy-950/40 border-t border-slate-200 dark:border-navy-800 text-center">
    <p class="text-xs italic text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 m-0">In a trust, “who owns,” “who holds” and “who is assessed” can be three different legal questions.</p>
  </div>
</div>
